            <ArticleTitle>A displaced acetabular component causing femoral neck notching following hip resurfacing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>321-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the case of a patient who developed a notch on the femoral neck following a hip resurfacing operation as a result of a displaced acetabular component. The acetabular cup displaced in the coronal plane and impinged on the femoral neck leading to a large notch in the inferior femoral neck.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
